From: Lauri Ahonen <lauri.ahonen@diktamen.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/http: match "close" as a Connection token

Backport of the fix submitted to ffmpeg-devel. Identical implementation, so this
file can simply be dropped once it lands upstream.

RFC 9110 defines Connection = #connection-option (Section 7.6.1), and the #rule
list extension (Section 5.6.1) expands that to elements separated by a comma and
optional whitespace. The "close" token was compared against the entire field
value, so it was only detected when it appeared as the sole option.

Apache with mod_http2 answers "Connection: Upgrade, close" alongside
"Upgrade: h2,h2c", which no longer matches. s->willclose stays 0, the connection
is treated as reusable, and the next request - the seek used to size the file -
is written into a socket the server has already closed:

    [https @ ...] Error reading HTTP response: End of file

avio_size() then yields nothing, so the mp3 demuxer cannot check the Xing/Info
byte count against the file size and reports

    [mp3 @ ...] invalid concatenated file detected - using bitrate for duration
    Duration: N/A

which made a 2 minute recording play for half a second with duration 0. Any
proxy that appends a token to the header trips this the same way.

diff --git a/libavformat/http.c b/libavformat/http.c
--- a/libavformat/http.c
+++ b/libavformat/http.c
@@ -1288,8 +1288,20 @@
         } else if (!av_strcasecmp(tag, "Proxy-Authenticate")) {
             ff_http_auth_handle_header(&s->proxy_auth_state, tag, p);
         } else if (!av_strcasecmp(tag, "Connection")) {
-            if (!strcmp(p, "close"))
-                s->willclose = 1;
+            /* RFC 9110 defines Connection = #connection-option (Section 7.6.1),
+             * and the #rule list extension (Section 5.6.1) expands that to elements
+             * separated by a comma and optional whitespace. Comparing the whole
+             * field value therefore only detects "close" when it is the sole
+             * option. Empty elements are skipped, as Section 5.6.1.2 requires. */
+            char *saveptr = NULL, *next = p, *token;
+
+            while ((token = av_strtok(next, ",", &saveptr))) {
+                next = NULL;
+                token += strspn(token, " \t");
+                token[strcspn(token, " \t")] = '\0';
+                if (!av_strcasecmp(token, "close"))
+                    s->willclose = 1;
+            }
         } else if (!av_strcasecmp(tag, "Server")) {
             if (!av_strcasecmp(p, "AkamaiGHost")) {
                 s->is_akamai = 1;
